# Hemal Trainer Management System

This plan outlines the steps to build the web-based system for the "Hemal Trainer Management" application based on the provided starter code specifications. The project will consist of a Node.js/Express backend and a React (Vite) frontend.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Selection:** The specifications call for a PostgreSQL database. 
> - Do you already have a PostgreSQL database running locally or remotely (like Supabase/AWS)? 
> - If you want to get up and running quickly without installing PostgreSQL, we can use **SQLite** for the initial development phase and migrate to PostgreSQL later. Please confirm which database you would like to proceed with.

> [!WARNING]
> **Scope of Work:** The specification includes a Flutter mobile app. Since you requested to "create webbasesystem", this plan currently only covers the **Backend API** and the **Web Admin Panel (React)**. If you also need the Flutter mobile app initialized, please let me know.

## Proposed Changes

We will create a monorepo structure with `/backend` and `/frontend` folders.

### Backend Application (`/backend`)
We will initialize a Node.js application and implement the core REST APIs for the management system.

#### [NEW] `backend/server.js`
- Core Express application setup, configuring CORS and JSON middleware.
- Routing for `/api/employees`, `/api/trainings`, `/api/ojt`, and `/api/auth`.

#### [NEW] `backend/config/db.js`
- Database connection configuration.

#### [NEW] `backend/routes/employees.js`
- API endpoints to fetch and create employees.

#### [NEW] `backend/routes/trainings.js`
- API endpoints to fetch and create training sessions.

#### [NEW] `backend/routes/auth.js`
- JWT authentication endpoint for login.

### Web Admin Panel (`/frontend`)
We will use Vite with React and Tailwind CSS to create a modern, responsive web dashboard with a premium aesthetic.

#### [NEW] `frontend/package.json`
- Initialize Vite project and install dependencies (axios, react-router-dom, tailwindcss, lucide-react for icons).

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/index.css`
- Tailwind directives and custom design tokens for a rich, modern aesthetic.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/App.jsx`
- Main application routing using `react-router-dom`.

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx`
- A visually impressive dashboard showing key metrics (Employees, Trainings, Pending, Completion rate).

#### [NEW] `frontend/src/pages/Employees.jsx`
- A data table view to list and manage employees.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- We will verify that the backend server starts successfully and can connect to the database.
- We will verify that the React frontend builds and starts locally without errors.

### Manual Verification
- We will start both the frontend and backend servers.
- The web app should load at `http://localhost:5173` showing the modern Hemal Trainer Management Dashboard.
- We will test API connections by navigating to the Employees page and ensuring data flows correctly from the backend to the frontend.
